From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qa <qa@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:29:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] profile: an unchecked precondition outranks a known
 limitation

Verdict.severity ranked PARTIAL above UNKNOWN. HostProfile.verdict takes
the maximum, so a host with one limitation (no access to the render node)
and one fact nobody could check (no session, KVM not probed) came out
PARTIAL - "it could run" - and `lynxdroid profile` exited 0, while
`lynxdroid doctor --strict` exited 6 for the same machine. The docstring
of `verdict` already promised the opposite: "one unknown keeps the answer
unknown even if everything else passed".

The order is now READY < PARTIAL < UNKNOWN < BLOCKED.

The defect predates the Waydroid removal. It was not visible on the
sandbox because that host has unknowns but no limitation to combine them
with; it shows up as soon as doctor and profile are compared on described
hosts that differ in two facts, which is what the three new cases do.
With the old order they fail:

  test_unknown_outranks_a_limitation
  test_doctor_and_profile_agree_on_a_described_host[limitation-plus-no-session]
  test_doctor_and_profile_agree_on_a_described_host[limitation-plus-kvm-unprobed]

pytest: 1060 passed, 1 skipped (1061 collected).

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
