+A second one was found on 2026-11-10 and is why that test now also runs both
+commands against nineteen *described* hosts. `Verdict.severity` ranked
+`PARTIAL` above `UNKNOWN`, so a machine with one known limitation (no access
+to the render node) and one fact nobody could check (no session) came out
+`PARTIAL`: `profile` exited 0 where `doctor --strict` exited 6. The live host
+never showed it, because the sandbox has no limitation to combine with its
+unknowns. The order is now `READY < PARTIAL < UNKNOWN < BLOCKED`, and
+`doctor` requires the same five facts the profile judges (`gpu.device` and
+`session.display` were not required before).
